A||N||6||bHooper||ordered new shocks, and suspension update||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||12-05-2000||05:06 PM||||i just had to share the excitement with someone else... partly because I am dying to get my car back on the street (it's been a 2 month suspension job) and I need someone to tell me it's ok.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>i called the order in to Carparts, and was able to use the 33% off coupon, again.  apparently, if you've used it once, and give em a different email, you can get by with it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>originally, i had purchased cheap Monroe front shocks ($11 ea) and Gabriel Springfield rear struts ($30 ea), but i decided that this would not offer the performance that i wanted... especially with the Eibach springs!<P>as a update on my suspension rebuild.  i have done the following:<P>*steering rack ($114, Autozone)<BR><B>all</B> bushings are now poly ($ 100 nopi)<BR>*Moog front upper ball joints ($34 ea, wrenchead)<BR>*Carquest front lower ball joints ($34/pair)<BR>*rear ball joints ($? partsamerica)<BR>*new outer tie rod ends ($30 ea, partsamerica)<BR>*monroe steering stabilizer ($27, partsamerica)<BR>*Moog adjustable cam bolts ($14 ea, wrenchead)<BR>*new rear hub/bearing assemblys ($51 ea, partsamerica)<BR>*Eibach springs ($212, Carparts (w/33%off))<BR>*turned rear rotors (thanks Fieroshop!)<BR>*new rear calipers ($32 ea, autozone)<BR>*KYB shocks/struts ($137, Carparts (w/33%off)<P>and thats all i can think of, at the moment... seem like the credit card has taken a larger hit than that.  maybe not.<P>i will still have to purchase new tires, and possibly rims, at some point... so thats another $g...<P>anyway, all in the name of improved handling.  if i build the car i want, i will ultimately be happy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>thanks for reading my ramblings!<P>hoop<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-05-2000||05:59 PM||||Hoop deserves some at-a-boys!  If it even remotely needed to be replaced, it was gone!<P>I look forward to riding in it when it is on it's wheels, since I got to try it before the major work.<P>You need to drive it to the get-together at Golden Corral on the 16th.  Hopefully we will have a crowd gathered to admire your work!<P>Has the fuel line arrived yet!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||the need for speed||12-05-2000||06:30 PM||||hey hooper do you have part numbers||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||12-05-2000||09:36 PM||||part numbers... give me a bit to assemble em, and i will post that.<P>thanks Bob!  really, truth be know, if it hadn't been for you i would have never done all this work! i mean, i could'nt stand myself if i took a ride in your car and then had to go home in mine!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  it all started with a ride in that Formula of yours, back in the spring!  it took that for me to get my own car running!<P>besides, i've been saying i'm gonna do it... so i finally did!<P>hoop<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 12-05-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||bHooper||12-06-2000||01:58 PM||||ok, so ya want part numbers.  i will include, source, part number, qty and price.<P><B>Wrenchead</B><BR>*Moog slotted Upper ball joint, MOO K5292, qty-2, $32.11 each<BR>*Moog Cam & Pivot bolt, MOO K5283, qty-2 sets, $13.31 each<P>Wrenchead had a $25 off coupon at the time, so my total was $74.<P><B>Partsamerica</B><BR>*Monroe steering stabilizer, qty-1, $26.99<BR>*Front Tie Rod end, ES2232R, qty-2, $41.99<BR>*Rear Tie Rod end, ES2255R, qty-2, $32.99<BR><B>it should be noted that i could not discern any difference between the 2 sets of tie rod ends</B><BR>*Rear wheel hub/bearing assembly, S513011K, qty-2, $51.99 ea<BR>*Rear lower ball joint, FA1146, qty-2, $34.99<P>PA had a 25% off coupon, at the time, so my total was around $265!<P><B>Autozone</B><BR>*Steering rack, Atsco, gty-1, $114.99 ($50 core)<BR>*rt Rear brake Caliper, C274, $31.99 ($80 core)<BR>*lt Rear brake Caliper, C275, $31.99 ($80 core)<BR>*Rear brake pads, MKD262, $15.99<P><B>Carparts.com</B><BR>*Eibach springs, 3802.140, $274.63 for set of 4 springs<BR>*KYB Front Shocks, KG4538, qty-2, $28.85 ea<BR>*KYB Rear Struts, 234005, qty-2, $59.95 ea<P>The springs cost me $212, delivered, and the shocks and struts cost $137, delivered.<P>Carparts has a coupon good for 33% off (#1963005).  I was able to use this on both purchases (i did the springs online and called the KYB's in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P><B>Carquest</B><BR>Front lower ball joints, $34/pair<P>And thats about that.  It cost me $60 to have the machine shop press in the front ball joints, and upper control arm bushings, plus clean up a few parts.  In addition, I bought a used set of rear rotors from the Fieroshop.<P>Originally, I bought struts from AZ and shocks from Advance, so thats an additional $85 spent.  Hopefully, I can recover most of that by selling those, along with the factory springs.<P>So far this has cost me about $1300, add $60 for an alignment, and pray I don't need to buy tires right away  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hope this helps somebody, besides myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>hoop<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||12-07-2000||08:32 AM||||Wow!  What a job.<P>Thanks for part numbers.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||12-07-2000||11:16 AM||||thanks!<P>i didn't list the part numbers for the poly bushings because they are the same part numbers listed on the Prothane/Suspension Tech web site, as well as mentioned here on a thread in October.<P>i ordered them through NOPI, and they were drop shipped direct from Dee Engineering (parant to Prothane), and cost $100 total for the front and rear control arms, plus the cradle bushings.  Much cheaper than any other source!<P>hoop||||reg||1
